WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.720
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar and you're watching Mind Your Decisions

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.740
Start out with a square with a side length of one

00:00:08.349 --> 00:00:13.439
Draw another square, and then draw another square that connects to both of these squares

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.850
Finally draw a fourth square that is attached to this third square

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.460
We're going to construct a triangle

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:27.510
Well first draw the diagonal of the first square and then we'll connect it to this corner of the fourth square

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.949
The question is what is the area of this triangle?

00:00:33.309 --> 00:00:39.959
I Adapted this from a puzzle by Catriona Shearer who's on Twitter @Cshearer41

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.779
And I read it on the blog, Math With Bad Drawings

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:49.529
Can you figure it out? Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for a solution

00:01:03.879 --> 00:01:10.289
So, how can we solve this problem? Let's get a different perspective by rotating the entire diagram

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:19.500
Now, let's label some of the lengths

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.470
The small square has a side length of one

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:27.900
And the larger square will have a side length that's equal to two of these small squares.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.000
So, it'll be equal to two

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.569
The base of the triangle is along this line

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.369
Now, the height will be along the perpendicular to this line

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:43.500
And let's just create a little rectangular grid and by doing so,

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:52.469
We can see that the height of this triangle is along and exactly equal to the diagonal of the square with a side length of 2

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:57.239
So now let's calculate the base and height of this triangle

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.949
The base of this triangle is the diagonal of a square with a side length of one

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.350
So it's base will be equal to the square root of two

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:08.849
The height of the triangle is the diagonal of a square with a side length of two

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:12.299
so this length will be two times the square root of two

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.500
And now we figured out the important dimensions we need

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.700
The area of a triangle is equal to its base times its height all over two

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:28.330
We've calculated the base and we've calculated the height and this simplifies to be equal to two and that's our answer

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:35.830
Amazingly we can solve this problem without knowing the height of the fourth square. Did you figure it out?

